The municipality layer therefore divides Guajicutea into one small island district and sixteen mainland districts, with the densest urban municipalidades concentrated in the Waribá corridor and the Tabakurí–Barikú axis. The largest non-city municipality is [[Waku Bá]], while [[Yukubá]] remains the principal southwest municipal centre outside the city-tagged cluster system.

